  "caveats": [
    "Inputs are the margin, the clock, possession and the pregame prior only: no fouls, timeouts, bonus or lineups.",
    "The prior is a single number per game; injuries and rest after the line or rating are not seen.",
    "NBA trains on the spread prior; a lineless NBA game gets the rated prior, which the booster saw only through the spread's scale.",
    "WNBA trains on the weekly box-ratings prior and serves the possession-ridge rated prior: same scale, different estimator.",
    "Train and holdout seasons are whole seasons, so the holdout is out of sample in time but shares rules eras.",
    "The rated prior's constants were fit on other seasons, but the NBA penalty and probit scale were kept after a look at the 2024-2026 seasons the prior gate scores (nba_season_sim.PRIOR_CONSTANTS).",
    "The home-court baseline's constants were fit on 2024, a prior-gate season, which favours the baseline.",
    "The prior gate pools seasons; a single WNBA season is too small to clear two standard errors alone (gate_by_season).",
    "The rated prior is opt-in: score_win_prob and game_page_tables serve it only when the caller passes rated_home_prob; without it a lineless game gets home court alone."
  ]
